Let $X_1,\dots,X_n$ ($n\ge 2$) be independent $N(\mu,\sigma^2)$, with sample mean $\bar X$ and sample variance $S^2 = \frac1{n-1}\sum(X_i-\bar X)^2$. Then

1. $\bar X$ and $S^2$ are independent;
2. $(n-1)S^2/\sigma^2 \sim \chi^2_{n-1}$;
3. $T = \dfrac{\bar X-\mu}{S/\sqrt n} \sim t_{n-1}$.
